<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mathgamain mac Cennétig</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 976</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mathgamain mac Cennétig was king of the Dál Cais and, from about 970, king of Munster, the elder brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brian-boru">Brian Boru</a>. With Brian he defeated the Norse of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limerick">Limerick</a> at Sulcoit in 967 and sacked their town, and he took Cashel from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eoganachta">Eóganachta</a>. In 976 he was captured by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donnuban-mac-cathail">Donnubán mac Cathail</a> and killed by Máel Muad mac Brain, a rival claimant to Munster.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mathgamain-mac-cennetig.jpg" alt="Mathgamain mac Cennétig" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Fergus O'Hea · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brian_of_the_Tributes.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
